        Map<String, Long> colorCounts = cars.stream()
                .collect(Collectors.groupingBy(Car::getColor, Collectors.counting()));

        String mostPopularColor = colorCounts.entrySet().stream()
                .max((e1, e2) -> e1.getValue().compareTo(e2.getValue()))
                .map(Map.Entry::getKey)
                .orElse(null);

        long count = colorCounts.get(mostPopularColor);

        System.out.println("Most popular color: " + mostPopularColor);
        System.out.println("Count: " + count);
    }
}
```

In this example, we first group the `Car` objects by their color using the `groupingBy` collector. Then, we find the color with the maximum count using the `max` method. Finally, we print the most popular color and its count.

